{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1257265-hedge-denizen-goblin-queen-and-more-questions","id":1257265,"title":"Hedge Denizen, Goblin Queen, and more questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-09-25T14:49:19-07:00","id":1257265,"title":"Hedge Denizen, Goblin Queen, and more questions","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> I have a lot of questions about Changeling second edition:<br /> <br /> 1. Hedge Denizen: This condition grants you 3 contracts or dread powers if you are a mortal... How do you fuel them? Does it grant Wyrd and at what rating?<br /> 2. Hedge Denizen: What happens if you are a non-changeling and get this? You get Wyrd in addition to your power stat?<br /> 3. Goblin Queen: If you pick a child, what Wyrd does the child get? What happens to her when she comes of age?<br /> 4. Morality stat for Hobgoblins. What do they use? The examples on the book lack a morality stat, when needed one (certain powers of other splats) what do they use?<br /> 5. Mantle and Court Goodwill: Does a Court Goodwill allow use of the court method of harvesting Glamour? Does it grant any effect on the Changeling's mien?<br /> 6. Fae-Touched: Can a creature with a template become one?<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 09-26-2018, 10:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-26T06:49:46-07:00","id":1257354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1257265-hedge-denizen-goblin-queen-and-more-questions#post1257265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> <br /> I have a lot of questions about Changeling second edition:<br /> <br /> 1. Hedge Denizen: This condition grants you 3 contracts or dread powers if you are a mortal... How do you fuel them? Does it grant Wyrd and at what rating?<br /> 2. Hedge Denizen: What happens if you are a non-changeling and get this? You get Wyrd in addition to your power stat?<br /> 3. Goblin Queen: If you pick a child, what Wyrd does the child get? What happens to her when she comes of age?<br /> 4. Morality stat for Hobgoblins. What do they use? The examples on the book lack a morality stat, when needed one (certain powers of other stats) what do they use?<br /> 5. Mantle and Court Goodwill: Does a Court Goodwill allows the use of the court method of harvesting Glamour? Does it grant effect on the Changeling's mien?<br /> 6. Fae-Touched: Can a creature with a template become one?<br /> Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>6. No, except maybe wolf blooded<br /> 5. I think so<br /> 4. Human Hobgoblins use Integrity, and Changeling Hobgoblins use Clarity, the rest don't have a morality (hypothetically a mage or vampire could gain a Hedge Denizen or maybe Goblin Queen conditions, they would retain their usual morality trait).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T10:40:30-07:00","id":1257601,"title":"","content":"1, it isn't explicitly said but as it doesn't list gaining Wyrd I'd say you might have to rely on catches. Or if you gave the dead power bottle glamour you could make use of that, or trade for another's bottled glamour.<br /> <br /> 2, as it doesn't say it grants wyrd you wouldn't grant wyrd. Mostly, same as above. <br /> <br /> 3, refer to 1<br /> <br /> 4, lists no change to morality so whatever they previously have. <br /> <br /> 5, I'm not sure on the RAW here but personally I wouldn't allow it but I might be wrong. <br /> <br /> 6, with how it's structured to use integrity I'd say it likely is intended as mortal only which fits a minir template. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, personally I feel that a hedge denizen should be able to store glamour at least as well as a fae touched Wyrd 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-27T14:09:05-07:00","id":1257645,"title":"","content":"1. &amp; 2. &amp; 3. I suspect an oversight in not mentioning Wyrd 1 for a conversion. The section on Hobgoblins declares that they have a minimum of 1, though, so I'd use that. When the child comes of age, they &quot;ascend the throne&quot;, which sounds like they have the merit prior, but it doesn't grant rule. At majority, they begin to rule. The example in the book (p258-9) is clearly on the throne already and has Wyrd 2. She's not at the age of majority in modern cultures, but...<br /> 4. Seems like they either retain what they had or lose it for the duration. If the latter, many of the powers would end with a &quot;Does not apply&quot;. You could, if you interpret things thataway but want <i>some</i>thing, use Wyrd.<br /> 5. Harvesting rules specify Court, not Court Goodwill or Mantle, so just your court.<br /> 6. It's obvious that the intent is base humans. Wouldn't wreck anything to allow others, really, but anything that isn't &quot;human&quot; violates the RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}